WHY MONITORING IS REQUIRED

Resource Tracking - We need to know CPU, memory, and other resource usage at all times, just like Task Manager on a laptop. Without it, we cannot take action on problems.

Log Preservation - In Kubernetes, if a node goes down and gets recreated (auto-scaling), logs inside that node get deleted. We lose troubleshooting data.

Scale Problem - In large environments (100+ machines), manually checking logs on each machine is impossible.

Security - Hackers can enter a system and delete logs. Without a backup, we never know what happened.

Storage Problem - Keeping all logs on application servers makes machines heavy and costly.

SOLUTION: Centralized Monitoring System

Keep all logs in a centralized location. Benefits:

Machine goes down? Logs are still safe centrally.
100 or 1000 machines? All logs in one place.
Attacker detected? Alerts triggered to security/L1 teams automatically.
No heavy machines needed for individual servers.
