MONITORING TYPES COVERED

Infrastructure Monitoring - Covers CPU, memory, disk, network, VMs, containers, on-premises servers. An agent collects data, analyzes it, and visualizes/reports it.

Application Monitoring - Covers application logs, access logs, APIs, SLAs, transactions, performance, error logs, user response metrics, network traffic.

Network Monitoring - Covers throughput, input/output, packet loss, data loss. Often uses SNMP or APIs since agents cannot be installed on network devices.

